    {
      "id": "context-2",
      "page": 7,
      "text": "Many unexplored questions surround the optimal knowledge representation and reasoning modalities for multi-hop QA. In this section, we conduct an extensive ablation study to validate the core components of ThreadRAG and summarize key findings.",
      "box": [
        0.1190314128236314,
        0.549861672308235,
        0.4887661948573394,
        0.629855296918665
      ],
      "precision": "text_fragment"
    },
    {
      "id": "context-3",
      "page": 7,
      "text": "The STM preserves crucial contextual integrity. As shown in Table 2, removing the entire STM module (i.e., SN and STG) and using LLMextracted triplets leads to a severe decline in performance, with the EM score dropping by 9.2% on MuSiQue. Furthermore, replacing our MLP-based Semantic Nodes (SN) with fixed-length chunks results in a noticeable 3.4% drop on HotpotQA. We attribute this to the fact that traditional triplet extraction or arbitrary chunking inevitably destroys the continuous narrative flow, resulting in irreversible semantic loss that hinders the LLM's ability to deduce complex answers.",
      "box": [
        0.1190314128236314,
        0.6309063263172149,
        0.4887661948573394,
        0.8401236819808466
      ],
      "precision": "text_fragment"
    }
